Pros:
+ Art style is fantastic;
+ Gameplay is fun and entertaining;
+ Easy to learn, hard to master;
+ Ankama support has improved from Wakfu ten fold;
Cons:
- PvE content has a 15 Kama fee but doesn't really pays off. (You get 5 Kama per win in normal PvP)
- If you like Eniripsa, you'll not have fun in the game at all it's starting deck is garbage and you will lose a LOT;
- Your game experience depends directly of which deck you choose to play;
- No balanced;
- Music, as in Wakfu is extremely repetitive;
- It may feel like a cash grab an hour in.
Obviously, you should make up your own mind about the game. I think it has potential as far as CCGs go, I think they need to focus a bit on non-paying players because want it or not, they are the majority of the player base. :P

